Third-party data (public-domain / freely redistributable U.S. Government works):

- NASA JPL Development Ephemerides (DE440) — the authoritative ephemeris. The kernel `de440s.bsp`
  (~32 MB) is NOT committed to this repository, but IS REDISTRIBUTED inside every release artifact
  (Windows .zip, Linux .tar.gz, and macOS .app under Contents/Resources). DE440/DE441 are works of
  the U.S. Government, not subject to copyright in the United States and freely redistributable,
  which is what makes bundling them possible. The shipped file is verified against a pinned SHA-256
  (crates/ephemeris/src/resolve.rs) before packaging, so what ships is what was reviewed.
  https://ssd.jpl.nasa.gov/planets/eph_export.html
- JPL Horizons Chiron ephemeris — sampled into the committed table crates/ephemeris/data/chiron.bin.
  https://ssd.jpl.nasa.gov/horizons/
- SEC EDGAR (Form 8-A listing dates) — used to enrich the stock seed. https://www.sec.gov/edgar
- Stock IPO dates originate from a Polygon.io-sourced dataset (public listing facts).
- Place data © GeoNames (CC BY 4.0) — the offline gazetteer in crates/geo (derived from the
  GeoNames cities5000 dump, preprocessed into the committed crates/geo/data/cities.bin).
